<cem:title lang="" subtitle="">Spices from South Asia</cem:title>
<cem:description lang="">This virtual learning object "Spices from South Asia" that makes part of the lesson No: 7, Vanessa in Cooking School: Indian Food which belongs to English teaching Elementary (A2.1), it is intended to work on: Ask for and give simple advice. The grammar of this LO is referred to Quantifiers: some, any, a little, few, e.g., I'd also like some ginger; Countable and uncontable nouns, e.g., Chili pepper, cinnamon stick, ginger; Why don't you ...?, e.g., Why don’t you try heating them in a frying pan?. Also, the vocabulary considers: Food and Drink, e.g., Chili pepper, cinnamon stick, ginger.</cem:description>
